		{
			"id": "TNn9GJ4CsTHfHmMso",
			"name": "Xenos Bane",
			"local_notes": "Alternative Abilities (B61): all five specialisations are listed, but only Tyranids is enabled (5 points, the shared cost of every child) — enable the child that fits the Marine's posting history instead and disable Tyranids; a GM may let a long-serving Black Shield enable a second for 1 more point (see the parent trait's own container note in Deathwatch.adq).\n\nLore: Deathwatch kill-teams are built and briefed around a specific, known threat far more often than a Chapter-side Marine ever is; a veteran who has hunted the same xenos race across a dozen postings develops a narrow, hard-won edge against it specifically, distinct from the broader Xenos Hunter Talent above. The Deathwatch RPG line builds an entire background/specialisation system around exactly this (a kill-team specialist's chosen xenological focus); this project's own division into five named banes is a reasoned approximation of that idea in GURPS terms, not a page-for-page reprint of any FFG table.\n\nDesign: Each bane is a small conditional combat/skill bonus (data-format.md's `conditional` feature) restricted to one named threat: +1 is a genuinely useful edge in exactly the fights this project's fiction says a specialist has trained for, without becoming a blanket combat bonus the way a general \"+1 to hit\" advantage would. Priced at 5 points by analogy with this project's other narrow, situational bonuses (compare the Ecclesiarchy's Social Regard at 2/level for a reaction bonus valid with one group only) — a combat-relevant +1 restricted to one enemy type earns a somewhat higher per-point rate than a reaction bonus, but nowhere near a general Weapon Master-style trait's cost. Built as alternative_abilities (data-format.md) since picking more than one at full price double-dips on the same specialist-training justification; the container's own notes cover the GM exception for a genuinely veteran Black Shield.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Deathwatch"
			],
			"container_type": "alternative_abilities",
			"children": [
