		{
			"id": "efWTSEA7ulfk3sG_v",
			"description": "Deathwatch Shotgun",
			"local_notes": "Not equipped by default; swap in for a close-quarters/breaching loadout.\n\nLore: An Astartes-scale combat shotgun favoured by kill-teams expecting close-quarters xenos-clearance work — boarding actions, hive-tunnel sweeps, void-ship breaches — where a boltgun's penetrator round is wasted overkill and a wider, close-range spread matters more than range or armour penetration. Its family of specialist shells (named here Cryptclearer, Xenopurge and Wyrmsbreath) follows the Deathwatch RPG line's own tradition of purpose-built shotgun Special Issue Ammunition for exactly this role; this project's specific names and effects are its own reasoned build on that idea, not a reprint of any single sourcebook's shell list.\n\nDesign: Built up from the human-scale Combat Shotgun (Solid Projectile Weapons.eqp, 6d pi+ buckshot / 8d pi+ slug) the same way the Astartes bolt pistols scale up from their human equivalents in Bolt Weapons.eqp: one clear step of dice for a bigger 8-gauge Astartes shell (buckshot 8d pi+, slug 10d pi+) rather than the same shell in a bigger housing. Exact dice distribution: buckshot penetrates flak (DR 30) on 30.5% of hits and never beats carapace (DR 70); slug penetrates flak on 79.5% of hits and likewise never beats carapace — this remains firmly an anti-infantry/anti-swarm weapon, not a power-armour threat, matching every source's treatment of shotguns in this setting. Cryptclearer trades range and Acc for one more die at point-blank choke (9d pi+, 57.6% vs flak at that range) rather than a wider spread; Xenopurge and Wyrmsbreath both sacrifice two dice of base shot (6d, matching the human Combat Shotgun's own buckshot figure) to carry a bio-toxin or incendiary payload, following the same \"reduced penetrator, added follow-up\" logic the Godwyn boltgun's Hellfire round uses, with Wyrmsbreath's burn ex follow-up built to answer the specific \"kills things that just grow back\" niche its name implies. Handling: an Astartes-scale weapon per the framework's rule that Astartes-pattern gear runs one step heavier and bulkier than its human counterpart — 15 lb loaded (vs. the human Combat Shotgun's 9 lb) and Bulk -5 (vs. -4). Min ST 12† (√(10×15)≈12.2) is far below the Astartes boltguns' ST 19+, reflecting that a shotgun's recoil, unlike a boosted mass-reactive bolt round, doesn't scale with the shooter's raw strength the same way — an Astartes at ST 30 fires it essentially unencumbered, while a very strong, augmented human could still shoulder it two-handed at a real but survivable penalty. Buckshot keeps the human Combat Shotgun's full-auto-capable RoF 3; every precision or specialist shell drops to RoF 1, the same per-mode logic the human Combat Shotgun entry already uses. Rcl is bumped one point above the human weapon's figures (2/3 vs. 1/2) for the bigger shell's added kick; Shots 10(3) sits one round above the human gun's 8-round tube for the larger frame.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes",
				"Deathwatch"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "1200",
			"base_weight": "15 lb",
